    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d812">

                <pb facs="0707" n="695" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg695"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867.24/312: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Turkey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Steinhardt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ankara</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-05-29T14:00:00+03:00">May 29, 1942—2
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 8:25 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>499. My 434, May 16, 3 p.m.<anchor n="26" xml:id="d812-f1"/> Secretary General of
                    Foreign Office told me informally last night that Council of Ministers has given
                    its formal approval to new procedure with regard to furnishing of supplies to
                    Turkey and that he expected to transmit written notice to foregoing effect to
                    American and British Embassies prior to June 3d.</p>
                <p>Immediately upon receipt of formal notification from Ministry of Foreign Affairs
                    that new procedure has been accepted by Turk Government and unless instructed by
                    Department to contrary British-American Coordination Committee will commence to
                    function in cooperation with Turk Coordination Committee.</p>
                <p>I anticipate telegraphing Department next week Embassy’s recommendations
                    concerning several subjects which in my opinion should be considered in any
                    master lend-lease negotiations Department may inaugurate.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Steinhardt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
